BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bereza/Beryoze: Old Ukrainian and Yiddish songs in a new song cycl
 e from Zozulka Trio — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261020T183000
DTSTAMP:20261020T114413Z
UID:b44e98d5ba577e20884e985d851b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:6:30pm Doors\, 7:00pm Performance Free and open to the public 
 Many old songs brim with ecological awareness. Songs from the territory of
  modern Ukraine tell stories about plants like the birch tree– bereza in
  Ukrainian\, beryoze in Yiddish–that bend\, break\, and heal\, becoming 
 metaphors for human fragility and tenacity. Birds mark the turning of seas
 ons and shifts in our internal weather as well. Since 2011\, Zozulka —a 
 trio named after the Ukrainian word for cuckoo bird—has interpreted song
 s from a wide range of Ukrainian village traditions. With BEREZA / BERYOZE
 \, the trio branches into a new cycle of songs that speak directly to ecol
 ogical themes. In this project\, Zozulka reaches into Yiddish \nCategory: 
 Academic\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/live/events/332262
 -berezaberyoze-old-ukrainian-and-yiddish-songs-in-a
LOCATION:Wu Performance Hall\, Department of Music\, UC Berkeley\, Wu Perf
 ormance Hall\, Department of Music\, UC Berkeley
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/live/events/332262-berezaberyoze-old-ukrai
 nian-and-yiddish-songs-in-a
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
